/-!
Hand pass `GrindOrd` (hand13): 142 unresolved hypotheses of the ordered-algebra part of grind:
`Init.Grind.Ordered.Ring` (44), `Ordered.Field` (40), `Init.Grind.Order` (19), `Ordered.Linarith` (17),
`Ordered.Module` (17), `Ordered.Order` (5). Almost all are instance hypotheses: `IsPreorder`,
`LawfulOrderLT`, `OrderedAdd`, `OrderedRing`, `NoNatZeroDivisors`, plus a few certificate premises.

135 necessary, 7 removable, 0 independent, 0 left unresolved.

Necessary verdicts prove `¬ drop0% T i` (or `¬ indep0% T i` for the 15 dependent `IsPreorder` binders,
which `OrderedAdd`/`OrderedRing` take as a class parameter) by applying the hypothetical statement to
one of the models below and evaluating with `decide +kernel`. Removable verdicts prove `drop% T i`.

Reusable models (namespace `GrindOrdHand`; each a type synonym or structure with all the instances
it satisfies, plus `DecidableEq`/`DecidableLE`/`DecidableLT`):
* Int, lawful `<` from a broken `≤`: `IPle` (`≤` is `=` plus `1 ≤ 0`; preorder, no `OrderedAdd`),
  `IRev` (reversed order; linear, `OrderedAdd`, no `OrderedRing`), `IL2` (usual order with `2` the
  least element; linear, no `OrderedAdd`), `IGt` (`≤` and `<` both `>`; `IGt.not_preorder`).
* Int, usual `≤` (or reversed), `OrderedRing`, `<` not lawful: `ILTpos` (`a < b ∧ 0 < b`),
  `ILTodd` (`b - a` odd positive), `ILTall` (always true), `ILTnn` (`a < b ∧ 0 ≤ b`), `ILT01`
  (`a < b ∧ (a = 0 → b = 1)`: `1` is the only positive element, so the multiplication laws are
  trivial), `IRevLT` (reversed `≤`, usual `<`).
* `NSucc`: Nat with `a ≤ b := a = b ∨ b = a + 1` (reflexive, not transitive), lawful `<`.
* `F2T`: `Fin 2` with `≤` and `<` always true: preorder and `OrderedRing` of characteristic 2
  (`F2T.not_charP0`).
* Rat fields: `RLTge1` (usual `≤`, `a < b := a + 1 ≤ b`, `OrderedRing`), `RLTne` (usual `≤`,
  `<` is `≠`, `OrderedRing`: in a domain `≠` is preserved by multiplication with nonzero elements),
  `RRev` (reversed lawful order, no `OrderedRing`), `RLh` (usual order with `1/2` the least element).
* `CI`: the Gaussian rationals `ℚ(i)` as a grind `Field`, with the lexicographic order (imaginary part
  first; translation invariant and linear) and `a < b` iff `b - a` is a positive rational
  (`OrderedRing`, `<` not lawful): `0 ≤ i` but `i⁻¹ = -i < 0`. Over `ℚ` every translation-invariant
  linear order is the usual or the reversed one, and both satisfy `inv_nonneg_iff`/`inv_nonpos_iff`,
  so these two rows need a larger field.

Removable (7): `IsPreorder` of `Order.le_eq_false_of_lt`, `Order.lt_eq_false_of_lt`,
`Order.lt_eq_false_of_le`, `Preorder.not_ge_of_lt`, `Preorder.not_gt_of_lt` (each conclusion follows
from `a < b ↔ a ≤ b ∧ ¬ b ≤ a` alone), and `LawfulOrderLT` of `OrderedRing.mul_neg_of_pos_of_neg`,
`OrderedRing.mul_neg_of_neg_of_pos` (instances of the `OrderedRing` fields `mul_lt_mul_of_pos_left/right`).

The necessary declarations are generated by `runs/hand13/scratch_GrindOrd/gen.py`.
Run with the lean4 repo's stage1 binary: `runs/hand13/lean.sh checks/GrindOrdHand.lean`.
